 "about_text": "Espace Louis Vuitton Tokyo is a non-commercial exhibition space inaugurated in 2011, occupying a glass box on the top floor of the Louis Vuitton building in Omotesando, designed by Japanese architect Jun Aoki. Rather than a gallery representing artists for sale, it functions as an art space encouraging the creation of new contemporary artworks, staging rotating exhibitions by international contemporary artists such as Yayoi Kusama and Rina Banerjee. It is linked to a sister space, Espace Louis Vuitton Osaka, and to the Fondation Louis Vuitton, reflecting Louis Vuitton's broader engagement with contemporary art. Admission is free, and the program emphasizes striking architecture as much as the art displayed within it.",
